"""
hilde export: a release of the package, its archive and signatures, made only when its tests and its version hold.

- Every module below src has its test file, the tests pass, and every exported function is called in a test.
- The version of hilde.toml must be newer than the newest tag and at least what the interface difference calls for.
- A break under a minor or patch version is refused with H1530, a version that is not newer with H1534.
- llms.txt and man/man3 are written from the interfaces; with C, c/ and the name of this system gets the generated C.
- signatures/vX.Y.Z.sig is the signify signature of the line h1: and the checksum of the tree, which hilde get checks.
- dist/ gets the tree as name-X.Y.Z.tar.gz and the signify signature of the archive beside it.

    let made: Got := exportPackage(".", "release.sec", false, "/usr/local/bin/hilde", 1793000000);
"""
import Pkg.Get (
    Got
);

module Pkg.Export is
    """
    Makes the release of the package at root with the secret key at
    keyPath, the C for this system when withC is true, and the compiler at
    compiler for the tests and the C; the manual pages are dated by
    seconds since the epoch.
    No contract: an I/O result: what the tests, git and the disk said.
    """
    generic [R: Region, K: Region, C: Region]
    function exportPackage(root: Span[Nat8, R], keyPath: Span[Nat8, K], withC: Bool, compiler: Span[Nat8, C], seconds: Int64): Got;
end module.
